{"version_id": 82, "article_id": 9, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Science Needs Fair Rules When Countries Fight", "title_zh": "国家之间有冲突时，科学合作需要更公平的规则", "topic": "science", "source": "nature", "source_url": "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03176-y", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/49705390741_8c22b1fd8a_b.jpg", "credit": "USDAgov · pdm 1.0 · via flickr"}, "published_date": "2026-10-06", "word_count": 140, "reading_minutes": 0.7, "lead": "Science can bring people together. But when countries have problems, scientists from some places face unfair treatment. Two researchers say we need better rules.", "lead_zh": "科学可以把人们聚在一起。但是当国家之间出现问题的时候，来自一些地方的科学家会受到不公平的对待。两位研究人员说，我们需要更好的规则。", "preview": "Science has always helped people work together across the world. Many people believed science was free from political problems. But now, glo", "preview_zh": "科学一直帮助世界各地的人们一起合作。很多人曾经相信科学不受政治问题影响。但是现在，全球紧张局势正在加剧。这正在改变科学家们相互合作的方式。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 72, "url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@6f046c1/content/audio/9/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 61.675, "size_bytes": 373824, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 159, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@6f046c1/content/data/versions/82.json", "paragraphs": ["Science has always helped people work together across the world. Many people believed science was free from political problems. But now, global tensions are growing. This is changing how scientists work with each other.", "A new problem is appearing. Where a scientist works is becoming a sign of their political identity. In other words, people may judge a researcher by their university or country, not by their work. This is not fair.", "Two researchers wrote about this issue. Emmanuel Chidiebere Edeh works at Shanghai University in China. Ehizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi works at Zhejiang Normal University in China. They say we need fairer rules for global science collaboration.", "The article appeared in Nature on 6 October 2026. It is a correspondence piece. The writers do not have any competing interests. They want to keep science open and fair for everyone."], "paragraphs_zh": ["科学一直帮助世界各地的人们一起合作。很多人曾经相信科学不受政治问题影响。但是现在，全球紧张局势正在加剧。这正在改变科学家们相互合作的方式。", "一个新问题正在出现。科学家的工作地点正在变成他们政治身份的标志。换句话说，人们可能根据研究人员所在的大学或国家来评判他们，而不是看他们的工作。这是不公平的。", "两位研究人员写了关于这个问题的文章。Emmanuel Chidiebere Edeh 在中国上海大学工作。Ehizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi 在中国浙江师范大学工作。他们说，我们需要更公平的全球科学合作规则。", "这篇文章于2026年10月6日发表在《自然》杂志上。它是一篇通讯文章。作者们没有利益冲突。他们希望科学对每个人保持开放和公平。"], "body": "Science has always helped people work together across the world. Many people believed science was free from political problems. But now, global tensions are growing. This is changing how scientists work with each other.\n\nA new problem is appearing. Where a scientist works is becoming a sign of their political identity. In other words, people may judge a researcher by their university or country, not by their work. This is not fair.\n\nTwo researchers wrote about this issue. Emmanuel Chidiebere Edeh works at Shanghai University in China. Ehizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi works at Zhejiang Normal University in China. They say we need fairer rules for global science collaboration.\n\nThe article appeared in Nature on 6 October 2026. It is a correspondence piece. The writers do not have any competing interests. They want to keep science open and fair for everyone.", "body_zh": "科学一直帮助世界各地的人们一起合作。很多人曾经相信科学不受政治问题影响。但是现在，全球紧张局势正在加剧。这正在改变科学家们相互合作的方式。\n\n一个新问题正在出现。科学家的工作地点正在变成他们政治身份的标志。换句话说，人们可能根据研究人员所在的大学或国家来评判他们，而不是看他们的工作。这是不公平的。\n\n两位研究人员写了关于这个问题的文章。Emmanuel Chidiebere Edeh 在中国上海大学工作。Ehizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi 在中国浙江师范大学工作。他们说，我们需要更公平的全球科学合作规则。\n\n这篇文章于2026年10月6日发表在《自然》杂志上。它是一篇通讯文章。作者们没有利益冲突。他们希望科学对每个人保持开放和公平。", "text": "Science has always helped people work together across the world. Many people believed science was free from political problems. But now, global tensions are growing. This is changing how scientists work with each other. A new problem is appearing. Where a scientist works is becoming a sign of their political identity. In other words, people may judge a researcher by their university or country, not by their work. This is not fair. Two researchers wrote about this issue. Emmanuel Chidiebere Edeh works at Shanghai University in China. Ehizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi works at Zhejiang Normal University in China. They say we need fairer rules for global science collaboration. The article appeared in Nature on 6 October 2026. It is a correspondence piece. The writers do not have any competing interests. They want to keep science open and fair for everyone.", "vocab": [{"word": "science", "pos": "noun", "zh": "科学", "note": "不可数名词"}, {"word": "collaboration", "pos": "noun", "zh": "合作", "note": "常与 global 连用"}, {"word": "global", "pos": "adj", "zh": "全球的", "note": "指全世界"}, {"word": "fair", "pos": "adj", "zh": "公平的", "note": "反义词 unfair"}, {"word": "rules", "pos": "noun", "zh": "规则", "note": "复数形式"}, {"word": "researcher", "pos": "noun", "zh": "研究人员", "note": "指做研究的人"}, {"word": "university", "pos": "noun", "zh": "大学", "note": "常见机构名词"}, {"word": "political", "pos": "adj", "zh": "政治的", "note": "与 politics 相关"}], "title_original": "Maintaining global science collaboration during conflict requires fairer rules", "summary_original": "Nature, Published online: 06 October 2026;\ndoi:10.1038/d41586-026-03176-y\nMaintaining global science collaboration during conflict requires fairer rules", "body_original": "CORRESPONDENCE\n06 October 2026\nMaintaining global science collaboration during conflict requires fairer rules\nBy\nEmmanuel Chidiebere Edeh\n0\n&\nEhizuelen Michael Mitchell Omoruyi\n1\nEmmanuel Chidiebere Edeh\nShanghai University, Shanghai, China.\nView author publications\nSearch author on:\nPubMed\nGoogle Scholar\nEhizuelen Michael Mitchell Omor